linear regression

when we have single input we say it as simple linear regression if we have multiple input we say it as multiple linear regression.

in simple linear regression we try to create a best fit lines between the true points. so when a new input comes it can be easily predicted.

-> h0(x)=0o + 01.x equation of straight line used for only 1 feature. it can also be used for multiple feature where we expand 0 till n.

x = independent feature the x axis
0o= dependent feature y axis
01= slop. the increase of x axis value while increase of y axis value is slop .
h0(x)= predicted point = we can also write y^

when ever a new weight comes. we predict its height by using best fit line and to know the expected error in prediction we subtract y(original height) - y^(predicted height)
the difference came is error. and the sum of all error should be minimal least.
if there is another best liune which give lower minimal error after summing all errors we will choose that best fit line.
so in simple linear regression our main is to find best fit line and predict the result, the result is predicted by the model using simple linear reg eq.

